<h1>Insert Standard Pages</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-US">This command is accessible from</span> <b><i><span class="Path" style="font-style:normal; font-weight:bold;"><b>Pages &gt; Insert Standard Page</b></span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-style:normal; font-weight:bold;"><b>s</b></span></i>in</b> <span lang="EN-US" style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Inspection</u></span> <span lang="EN-US">mode.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">This command inserts 6 pages in the report pages list, containing all predefined views (except Isometric) of the inspected object. The pages have the same names as the standard views:</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Up</b></span><span lang="EN-US">,</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Down</b></span><span lang="EN-US">,</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Left</b></span><span lang="EN-US">,</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Right</b></span><span lang="EN-US">,</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Front</b></span><span lang="EN-US">,</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Back</b></span><span lang="EN-US">.</span></p>
<p class="USE"><span lang="EN-US">This command is useful for making quick report of the inspected object in predefined view positions.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Related topic:</b></span> &#160;<a href="Create_Page.htm">Create Page</a></p>
